🪤 **F-1675-1 (s1675 2026-08-11, MEASURED ON THE SEVENTH CONSECUTIVE HELD FIRE WHILE PRE-FLIGHTING THE DRAIN ITS FOUR PREDECESSORS PRESCRIBED — THE PENDING LANE-A DRAIN NEEDS A FRESHNESS PRE-CONDITION, BECAUSE BOTH OF ITS FAILURE MODES ARE SILENT AND THE WORSE ONE REVERTS MAIN. NOT AN OWNER QUESTION; DOES NOT JOIN THE DESK.)** 📋 **HOW IT SURFACED:** the board was dry and held for the seventh fire running, so — following the s1672 precedent of spending a held budget on the drain it is forbidden to perform — I asked the one question four next-fire instructions never asked: *when lane-a frees, will `git checkout lane/a -- <paths>` actually find anything there?* 📐 **MEASURED, read-only git plumbing, zero load on the running lane:** `lane/a`'s tip is **`031b61ff4` (2026-08-11T13:36:40)** — which is **s1657's own handoff commit**, not a runner commit: `ahead=0`, an **ancestor of main**, **91 behind**. **After 8h20m the 13:35 run has committed NOTHING.** And both deliverables are **byte-identical on lane/a and main** (`e30c810d…` 139,159 B · `51399654…` 2,358,427 B), so `git diff main lane/a -- logs/suite-red-inventory.md logs/suite-red-inventory-compact.json` is **EMPTY**. 🪤 **MODE 1 — SILENT NO-OP (what the recipe does TODAY):** the prescribed `git checkout lane/a -- <the two paths>` returns **rc=0, no output, zero diff**, i.e. a Silent No-Op (Mistake #1) wearing a successful path-scoped drain's costume — and the recipe's very next step flips the leaf `queued`→`merged` with a 40-char `mergeHash`, **recording a merge of nothing**. ⚠️ **MODE 2 — SILENT REVERT OF MAIN, worse and reachable:** proved by manufacturing it in a throwaway `/tmp` repo — when the ancestor's blob DIFFERS, `git checkout <ancestor-branch> -- path` **stages the OLDER content** (`M f.txt`), rc=0, no output: a regression of main dressed as a drain. **`lane/a` is 91 commits behind main, so only the accident that none of those 91 touched these two paths keeps us in mode 1 rather than mode 2.** 🔍 **WHY THE E