83 file(s)`.** Guarded by two more cases in `scripts/salvage-art-staging-reach.test.mjs` (now **10/10**), the red one PROVEN by manufacturing the directories-only enumeration and confirming it reaches the subdir file and NOT the root file. 💡 **AND THE GUARD EARNED ITS KEEP INSIDE THIS FIRE:** the F-1120-2 red-path mutation stopped applying the moment I rewrote the enumeration, and the test **failed loudly** (`mutation target absent — this guard has rotted`) instead of silently passing on a mutation that no longer manufactured anything. A red-path test that cannot notice its own rot is a green with extra steps.
🔺 **F-1640-1 (s1640 2026-08-10 — THE RETENTION LAW'S LARGEST HOLE FELL OFF THE OWNER'S DESK ~106 FIRES AGO AND NO FIRE NOTICED, BECAUSE THE INSTRUMENT THAT GUARDS THE DESK CANNOT SEE THIS FAILURE MODE BY CONSTRUCTION).** Found on a genuinely dry board by running `node scripts/art-staging-audit.mjs` — which **no rule obliged me to run**, since the ART-SLOT LAW keys that duty on TOUCHING the art slot and I did not. ✓ **RE-MEASURED LIVE, not inherited: AT RISK (in NO object database — dies with this disk) `583 files / 529.68 MB`; LOCAL-ONLY `0 files`** (nothing is merely unpushed; it is unstored). The desk rows carrying this hole state `748 files / 566.47 MB` (F-1331-4, F-1120-2) and its last update states `602 / 556.81 MB` (F-1350-1) — **all three figures are now stale**, so the numbers are restated on both rows rather than left to rot. 📉 **THE DIRECTION IS THE PART THAT NEEDS A WORD, AND I DELIBERATELY DID NOT GUESS IT: since s1350 the bucket has FALLEN by 19 files and 27.13 MB with no salvage recorded in between.** A shrinking at-risk bucket has exactly two causes and they are opposites — an **unrecorded salvage** (harmless) or an **untracked deletion** (a RETENTION LAW violation, the one thing the law names as forbidden). Resolving it retroactively needs a prior file list I do not have, so it is named as the open question rather than answered; the composition also changed (F-1350-1 records the bucket as *"entirely motion-pilot png/mp4"* with contact-sheets **gone** from it, yet today's at-risk listing shows `staging/contact-sheets` entries again — consistent with later art batches, but unverified). 🔑 **THE DROP-OFF, MEASURED IN STATUS ITSELF: `F-1120-2` was last carried on a handoff desk at **s1533**, `F-1331-4` at **s1435** — and neither appears on any desk since, including s1639's 16.** ⚠️ **WHY NO GUARD CAUGHT IT, which is the reusable half: `desk-state-audit` classifies the items you DID carry (`CLOSED`/`OPEN`/`BOTH`/`OPEN-DESK-ONLY`/`UNRECORDED`) — every one of its five categories presupposes the item is already on the line you hand it.** An item that silently **stops** being carried is therefore invisible to it, and it duly reported `CLOSED=0 · OPEN=0 · BOTH=0 · OPEN-DESK-ONLY=16 · UNRECORDED=0` for s1639 — a clean bill — while a 530 MB owner-gated item sat off the desk entirely. **That is F-1471-3's shape one level out: the desk guard fails OPEN, and what it fails open on is the SET, not the spelling.** ⓘ **HONEST LIMIT ON THE GENERALISATION — a screen is not a census, and mine was too crude to support one.** Counting BACKLOG rows whose line STARTS `- 🔺` gives 28 marked rows against 16 carried with only **3** ids in common, which looks alarming; but that key reports its hits and never its misses — **all 13 carried-without-a-🔺-row items DO have rows, under other markers (🟡/🟠/👑) or mid-line.** So the two registries genuinely diverge, but the size of the divergence is **UNMEASURED** and would need an instrument keyed on every marker spelling (the `drain-block-check` lesson: never conclude from one field name). Recorded as a signal worth an instrument, **not** as a measured defect. ✅ **ACTION TAKEN s1640: restored to the desk (16 → 17 carried), with the live numbers.** **GATE: OWNER — unchanged and still one word: salvage to a branch (the s1350 precedent, `save/art-staging-20260801`), accept the loss deliberately, or prune deliberately. No fire may take a 530 MB repo-size decision unilaterally (F-1103-2), and this fire did not.** ⚙️ **UPDATED s1658 (F-1658-1) — THE GATE IS UNCHANGED, BUT ONE OF ITS THREE OPTIONS WAS NOT EXECUTABLE UNTIL TODAY.** `salvage to a branch` names `scripts/salvage-art-staging.mjs`, and that script reached **0 of the 582 at-risk files** — it read only `worktrees/art/assets/raw`, non-recursively, while 100% of the exposure is nested under `motion-pilot/`. Answering *"salvage it"* would have produced a `save/*` branch holding 3 irrelevant files and a success line. **Fixed and guarded `c5d077cec` (8/8