🟢 **F-1641-1 (s1641 2026-08-10, MEASURED ON A BOARD THAT REPORTED ITSELF DRY, CURED THIS FIRE ON ALL FOUR SURFACES — AN OWNER RULING NAMED ITS OWN RESIDUAL GATE, AND THE SURFACE IT NAMED WENT ON REFUSING THE WORK FOR 36 FIRES. IT IS THE THIRD DIRECTION OF THE F-1279-1 / F-1614-1 CLASS, AND *BOTH* EXISTING GUARDS ARE BLIND TO IT BY CONSTRUCTION.)** 🧭 **HOW I FOUND IT:** s1640 handed forward **PIPELINE-DRY lanes a/b/c** with the reasoning *"blocked by file contention, not by absent spec"* — sound for the three nearest leaves, which it had cleared by measurement — but it named nine longer-horizon leaves it had **NOT** individually cleared. I walked those nine instead of inheriting the verdict (Mistake #4). ⚙️ **WHAT WAS WRONG:** the owner re-greenlit the AP ladder at the desk walkthrough, verbatim **"Greenlight all three"**, recorded `7e2b3e64b` (2026-08-09 21:45) as `tasks/BACKLOG.md`'s **`AP-03/04/05 RE-GREENLIT`** row — a row which correctly declares the leaves *"authorable again"*, correctly delegates the residual act (*"a fire flips its head with the confirming read"*), and correctly names the residual gate: **"GATE per leaf: its own spec."** ✗ **That spec — `specs/agent-play/README.md` — carried on its STATUS line, verbatim: *"AP-03/04/05 may not be authored or queued until the Saga Rehearsal delivers its verdict AND the owner re-greenlights."*** ⭐ **SO THE RULING ROUTED ITS OWN GATE INTO A SURFACE THAT REFUSED IT.** A fire obeying the ruling reads the gate; the gate forbids the work; per CLAUDE.md §7.2 (*verified conflict with a law → stop that action*) the correct, careful, law-abiding response is to **STOP** — and the greenlight becomes structurally unreachable through the very door it points at. ✓ **MEASURED, not inferred: the spec was last touched `a2b34fdb6` 2026-08-02 — a full WEEK BEFORE the ruling — and the desk-walkthrough commit `fc284845d` touched 5 files (`contracts.json`, `scripts/fire.md`, the mp-07c spec, `BACKLOG.md`, `goals.json`) and NOT this spec.** 📉 **THE COST: 36 distinct fire sessions and 41 handoff commits across ~24.3 h, with ZERO `ap-03`/`ap-04`/`ap-05` masters authored** (`ls tasks/ | grep ap-0[345]` → empty) — on a board that spent most of those fires declaring itself dry and hunting for authorable work. 🔒 **WHY BOTH GUARDS ARE BLIND, which is the reusable half.** (1) `scripts/ruling-propagation-guard.mjs` (F-1279-1) checks BACKLOG-says-RULED against **leaves that still refuse**, and its denominator is `leaf.status === 'blocked' || TERMINAL_CLOSED_STATUSES.has(...)` — **`ap-03/04/05` are `planned`, so they are excluded by construction**; run this fire it reports `3 findings recorded RULED · 31 goal leaves still refuse work · 0 stale · PASS`. (2) F-1614-1 built the mirror direction by hand (leaves freed while BACKLOG **declaring rows** kept refusing) — but here the declaring row is *correct*; the refusal is one hop further out. ⓘ **NEITHER GUARD READS `specs/**` AT ALL** — verified by reading the source: the guard opens exactly `tasks/goals.json` and `tasks/BACKLOG.md`. **The class is now three-sided: BACKLOG → goals.json (F-1279-1) · goals.json → BACKLOG (F-1614-1) · both → THE SPEC (this).** And the spec is the surface with the *strongest* claim on a fire's obedience, because §2E and the ruling itself both send you there. 🪞 **A SECOND SHAPE, MEASURED IN THE SAME PLACE AND WORTH ITS OWN NAME — THE SELF-CONTRADICTING STRING.** The walkthrough flipped the leaf titles by **appending** `— RE-GREENLIT (owner 2026-08-09…)` to titles whose bodies still read `DO NOT AUTHOR OR QUEUE` (`ap-04`) and `[REHEARSAL-GATED]` (`ap-05`). One string that both forbids and permits, with the prohibition **first**: a reader who stops at the imperative — which is what an imperative is for — never reaches the permission. **Appending a flip is not retiring the thing it contradicts.** ✅ **CURED THIS FIRE, ALL FOUR SURFACES, HISTORY RETAINED NOT DELETED (§4.10 / §6):** the spec head flipped to RE-GREENLIT with both halves cited and the old gate struck through as SUPERSEDED-DO-NOT-ACT · `ap-04` and `ap-05` titles retired their stale imperatives (2-line splice, `goals.json` re-parsed OK — never re-serialized) · the archived **`AGENT PLAY pace set`** row marked SUPERSEDED, kept because two other surfaces cite it by that exact grep key. 🚫 **DELIBERATELY NOT MECHANISED, following F-1614-1's own restraint and its explicit instruction to measure precision FIRST:** widening the guard to `specs/**` means parsing prohibition prose out of spec heads — a judgement surface, and judgement guards earn a permanent excused red (the `cross-engine` fate, F-1460-1). **The cheap discipline that would have caught it needs no mechanism: when a ruling names its own GATE surface, OPEN THAT SURFACE IN THE SAME FIRE — the ruling tells you where to look, in words, for free.** 💡 *Reusable shape: **a ruling is not delivered when it is recorded, it is delivered when every surface that can still say NO has stopped saying it** — and the last one to be flipped is reliably the one the ruling itself nominated, because naming a gate feels like discharging it.* ⚠️ **SCOPE, STATED HONESTLY: I did NOT clear the other six longer-horizon leaves** (`rf-04-bounty`, `rf-05-fixed-version`, `map-campaign-27`, `stream-live`, `ap-15-assay-of-minds`, `foundry-first-real-game`) beyond reading their titles — all six read owner-gated on their face (owner copy/prizes · owner vE1.0 tag + walk blessing · the 0/25 OWNER TEST column, whose leaf says in as many words *"Do NOT author a wiring or landmark master"* · owner starts the loop · spec DRAFT + 3 ratification Qs · owner brings the seed). **`bt-04-homestead-automation` I checked and it is NOT authorable** — F-1614-1 already ruled it *"unblocked as a **program** but still missing its four **parameters**"*, and the parameters (what X% is, what idle means) are exactly the design forks §7.3 reserves for the owner. **GATE: none owed to the owner — this is a bookkeeping propagation of a ruling