eep cannot see restores them as candidates **forever**, which is precisely the disease F-1600-1 named — *"a check that reports a discharged duty as owed reports it forever, and every fire pays the judgement cost again"* — and that cost is real: judging these six took the larger part of this fire's non-authoring budget. **Between a silent retirement and a permanent re-judgement tax, the retirement is the better failure, and it is at least written down.** ⓘ **WHAT WOULD ACTUALLY FIX IT, if a later fire wants it, is a purpose marker rather than a new file:** have the sweep count a hash as *dismissed* only when it appears on a line matching a declared marker (e.g. `NOT PLAYER-VISIBLE`), and report **two** numbers — reported *N*, dismissed *M*, candidates *K* — so the dismissals stay visible and re-judgeable instead of vanishing into the cited total. That is a ~10-line change to one script and it keeps every dismissal in the same file as the news it sits beside. **DO NOT build it as a red guard** — the same law bars that, and a WARN-level split is the whole ask. 📊 **Population, so the next fire knows the size of what is now invisible:** across the sweep's window (since 2026-08-05) **70 of 70** player-path-touching first-parent merges now read as cited; **four** of those are dismissals written this fire, and they are `6c780b621` (art run, premise spent and failed, artifacts + ledger only), `fc284845d` (desk walkthrough, ledger only), `f33380c92` (python verifier fix + scratch probes), `1a2871fd3` (delimiter re-encoding restoring grep over `Game.ts`). **GATE: none owed — this row is a pointer, not a debt.** A fire that wants the two-number split may build it under the WARN-level constraint above; a fire that does not need only know that a clean sweep is now a weaker signal than it looks. Related: [F-1600-1], [F-1546-1], [F-1599-1]. ✅ **CLOSED s1613 — the invited build LANDED: `f1612-1` merged `5624e6a7ff9633a61ac49c299da116f61f5759f0`.** This row's gate said *"none owed — 