2978-## Verification lessons (cumulative — s27 additions at top)
2979-- **s50: cp/`install -D` onto EXISTING tracked mount files FAILS (unlink denied) and the shell keeps going — the merge commit then silently misses every modified file.** Overwrite in-place with `cat source > target` (no unlink path), `cmp` to verify, and grep `git status` staged list against the slice inventory before committing. New files are unaffected. Same mount law family as s40's broken `git checkout --`.
2980-- **s27: `expect.poll`/`toPass` carry their OWN 5s default timeout — `test.setTimeout` does NOT feed them.** Any suite that "fixed" slowness with a test-timeout bump alone but polls past 5s is still broken (m2-03 was; audit new suites for this).
2981-- **s27: global renderer counters (info.memory.\*) are not pure functions of the system under test** — boot lazies land for seconds and vary run-to-run (baselines 9 vs 28, same build/machine). Assert cycle-correlated growth (quiesce → warm → grace cycle → zero-growth cycles), never absolute equality across a live window; per-frame `calls` compares as resting floors (min over a window), never instantaneous samples (1-2 frame post-swap transients).
2982-- **s27: sub-frame-gap visibility windows are protocol-invisible** — a 100ms fade completes inside one protocol round-trip at headless fps; only in-page rAF trackers armed BEFORE the trigger + monotonic counters (fadeWindow) observe them. s25's frame-gap law, applied to any transient overlay/flash assert.
2983-- **s27: vite dev SPA-fallback poisons existence probes** — fetch of a missing asset path returns 200 text/html; require an image/\* content-type. (The icons gate caught this on itself first run.)
2984-- **s27: stale `.last-run.json` can silently shrink a re-run's test set** — when a pass count looks short, re-run with full listing (`tail`), not `grep passed`.
2985-- **s27 env: dead sessions' /tmp dirs persist as nobody:700** — never reuse `/tmp/gr`; build in `/tmp/gr-sNN`. Neighbor load >2 → per-project serial playwright runs; m1-01 mobile splits ["spawns Claim Jumpers|nospawn blocks" / "double restart|stress=120"].
2986-- **s26: `net::ERR_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES` = browser-level refusal class (trace `status: -1`)** — chromium refuses random resource loads under VM degradation; app null-caches (loadProcessedTexture caches null FOREVER) → permanent placeholder for that cell until page reload. Forensics recipe: unzip the trace, `0-trace.network` per-line JSON → request url + response.status (-1 = refused). A/B on pure HEAD before blaming a slice — s26's whole failure set reproduced on HEAD. Bounded page-reload retry heals it (only null-cached cells re-request; HTTP cache serves the rest).
2987-- **s26: asset-dependent e2e must be lazy-load-aware** — cell textures load sequentially over seconds; never assert frameKeys from an eager fixed sample window after a direction flip. Pattern: in-page rAF collector with early exit on evidence-complete + generous deadline (vp-02 probe test is the reference).
2988-- **s26 env (this VM era): HOME SHARES the 99% /sessions disk — `~/gr` won't fit; build in `/tmp/gr`** (root disk, 3.2G free). Bare `/tmp/<file>` writes are Permission-denied — put logs INSIDE /tmp/gr. `timeout 40 npx playwright ...` inside the 45s bash wall keeps died-call zombies from eating a run's verdict. captureScreenshot can fail outright on the degraded compositor (retry once; else defer shots to the healthy sweep).
2989-- **s25: pin non-gated lanes to HEAD in ~/gr.** When another lane's output lands mid-gate, every rsync silently builds a COMBINED tree — after each mount→gr rsync, `git show HEAD:<file> > ~/gr/<file>` for all files belonging to lanes you are NOT gating, and re-run anything that executed after the leak window. Check `git status` against your triage inventory before EVERY commit — new modified files = a live lane.
2990-- **s25 env recipe (degraded-VM hour + disk):** `TMPDIR=/tmp` + `--trace=off` on every playwright call (Chrome profile + traces on /sessions crash pages at 99% disk); `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=/tmp/pw-browsers` explicitly per call (the ~/.cache symlink VANISHED mid-session once); npm cache at `/tmp/npm-cache` survives wipes; `rm -rf ~/gr/test-results` between batches; rsync `--exclude worktrees` ALWAYS (1.2GB on the mount). At ~6fps a protocol round-trip spans ~2 frames: any "sampled N times" or two-evaluate consistency assert is a coin flip — atomic one-evaluate samples or poll-the-tracker first (m2-02/m2-06 modernized `40b674a`; A/B on pure HEAD before touching any canary, 4 A/Bs run this fire, all env).
2991-- **s25: `| head` eats tsc's exit code** — `npx tsc 2>&1 | head -3; echo $?` reports head's status. Run `npx tsc; echo TSC-EXIT:$?` bare, or check output emptiness, and run it AFTER any e2e-file edit (Playwright transpiles without typechecking — a type-broken canary edit still "passes").
2992-- **s23: diagnostics singletons need additive contracts once a slot gains a second writer** — two `GeneratedSpriteBatch` instances on one slot id zeroed the shared `renderedSprites` count last-writer-wins (thief batch, usually empty, always wrote last). Fix pattern: per-writer contribution tracking, adjust-by-delta. Suspect this family whenever a "count stays 0 while the thing is plainly alive" symptom appears after a pooled-renderer split.
2993-- **s23: HUD-vs-state consistency asserts must be atomic (one in-page evaluate)** — sample-then-assert (`gold()` → `toContainText`) races live income at high timescale, and `toContainText`'s retry loop retries a STALE expected string. Chain overhead widened the gap enough to expose it (m2-02). Same family: assert-what-you-sampled, delta-from-event (m2-04 pathing fixed to delta-from-spawn this fire).
2994-- **s23: when a spec SANCTIONS a surface change, its canaries' assumptions need re-examination at the gate** — vp-02's fallback test blocked only the sheets it knew about; 008's rotation cells legitimately intercepted the fallback. Amend the canary to preserve its INTENT (block more, still demand the last fallback layer), never weaken it. Document in-file + in the review.
2995-- **s23 45s-wall updates:** m1-03 and m1-05 full files now exceed one bash call — m1-03 splits ["grace holds|wave banner|spawn accounting" / "alive cap|resetRun mid-wave"], m1-05 ["keyboard-build|registers kills|river placement" / "cost escalates|owner kills|harvest channel"]; m2-02 splits fine 3+["bank cap"]+["R rotates|four tappable"]; vp-02b runs per-test (8-direction and hysteresis ~19s each) and its shots test carries `test.setTimeout(60_000)`.
2996-- **s10: git on the mount leaves STALE `.git/HEAD.lock`/`index.lock`** when the Cowork delete guard blocks git's own cleanup ("unable to unlink … Operation not permitted" warnings on an otherwise-successful commit; the NEXT commit then fails "cannot lock ref HEAD"). Recipe: load+call `allow_cowork_file_delete` at first delete failure, `rm -f .git/HEAD.lock .git/index.lock`, retry. Check for stale locks at session start. Same guard blocks `git checkout --` restores of binaries until enabled.
2997-- **s10: renderer-memory gates must warm pool DEPTH, not just first use** — m1-02 texture assert failed 20→21 on clean HEAD on this slow VM: concurrent floats reach deeper float-text pool slots first-time DURING cycles (retained canvas upload; geoms stable). m1-05's warm-cycle pattern is now applied in m1-02 too (`0abbab2`). Suspect this pattern for any future "±1 texture/geometry" flake before blaming a slice.
2998-- **s10: this VM's /tmp SURVIVED re-provision** (chromium-1228 intact; only ~ was wiped) — check `/tmp/pw-browsers` before re-downloading. Heredoc gotcha: don't use `EOF` as delimiter in a bash call that also pipes another heredoc/multiline — a silent no-op patch resulted; use distinct delimiters (PYEOF) and assert-verify with grep after patching.
2999-- **s6 env variance:** VM home fully wiped (rebuild recipe worked; `.codex-auth/auth.json` on the mount is the auth seed); /sessions disk hit 100% (other tenants) → playwright browsers now live at `/tmp/pw-browsers` via `~/.cache/ms-playwright` symlink — RE-CHECK the symlink next session (/tmp wipes on VM restart); chromium fetched direct: `curl -C - https://cdn.playwright.dev/dbazure/download/playwright/builds/chromium/1228/chromium-linux-arm64.zip` (playwright install never fits the 45s wall). Background processes reaped ~60-90s (`setsid nohup` included): vite MUST start in the same bash call as its test batch — `fuser -k 5189/tcp; (npx vite --port 5189 --strictPort &) && sleep 3 && curl -s guard` then ONE batch <35s. This per-call kill+fresh-vite pattern also dodges s5's zombie-vite/stale-code hazard.
3000-- **Headless fps floor is a fiction under load: s6 saw 6fps** (vs s4's 17-22) — ALL throughput/visibility asserts must be in-page rAF trackers, never protocol polling (m1-02 hardened `93ddbae`; m1-06 was already right).
3001-- **Overlay `visible` lies:** hidden overlays are opacity-hidden → playwright counts them visible; `heroHp` is NOT a diagnostics key (`?? 100` guards made waits pass vacuously). Death waits: poll `state === 'dead'` or use the suite's `forceDeath`. Separation rings CAP contact DPS — huge point-blank packs form a donut and stall (~4 contacts/4s); overwhelm ≠ big pack, use forceDeath's repeated tight spawns.
3002-- **Probe-your-probe:** two s6 misdiagnoses (hit-pause "perma-freeze", "death never happens") came from polling nonexistent keys / protocol sampling. Verify the observable exists (`JSON.stringify` drops undefined silently) before trusting a 0.
